{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>These are the commandments.</b> No prophet is permitted to innovate anything further from now on." "<b>El the children of Israel.</b> After the pattern of ״ויצום אל בני ישראל״. <b>The order of the pericope Bechukotai is complete.</b> This book is called Torat Kohanim, because all the commandments pertain to the priest — such as the laws of offerings, and the dietary prohibitions, which involve ruling that is done by the priest, as it is written ״יורו משפטיך ליעקב״ etc.; and the laws of impurities and purities — not to eat anything impure, so as to be separated from entering the sanctuary; and the laws of the zav, the metzora, nega'im, those with a discharge, and women who have given birth; Sabbaths and festivals, in which there are offerings brought by the priest; and the laws of valuations, which the priests assess, and things declared herem, which the priests do; and the sabbatical year and the jubilee, in which the priests sanctify the years and blow the shofar on the jubilee, as it is written ״ובני אהרן יתקעו״ etc. And in Latin it is called Leviticus, after the book, which is Torat Kohanim, the sons of Levi — a play on words. <b>The book of Vayikra is complete. Praise to El Most High, awesome One.</b>"], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:53.030350013Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}